        },
        "head_input": {
          "type": "section_head",
          "settings": {
            "label": "04 · The input",
            "title": "Which is why MUTO works on the input, not the score.",
            "align": "center",
            "small": false,
            "tight": false
          }
        },
        "lede_input": {
          "type": "lede",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Three jobs, no overlap - produce NAD⁺, protect it from being broken down as fast as it is made, and give the cell what it needs to spend it. Every dose is at the level used in the research it comes from, printed in full on the label. No proprietary blends, no fillers, nothing you can’t check against your own stack.</p><p>There are no stimulants in it, so there’s nothing to feel in the first hour. What you’re buying is capacity, and capacity shows up in the data before it shows up as a sensation.</p>",
            "align": "left"
          }
        },
